
Get CPS - Quick docs...

----------------------
 WHAT THE HECK IS IT?
----------------------

This script will show the user the average CPS of their last transfer 
session after completion in BIG numbers.  It also keeps track of the
fastest (highest CPS) transfer for each baud and displays that as well.

It will also create a "down and dirty" Top CPS chart based on the
highest CPS rate to date regardless of baudrate.  This chart is a
normal ANSI file and will be written to the path/filename you set 
in the script. (Defaults to Zeus:Text/TopCPS.TXT)


--------------
 INSTALLATION
--------------

Real easy... goes into your File/PostXFer.zeus script (or whatever you 
call after a transfer is complete to show the results).  Install it in 
the script by inserting this one line at the start of the script AFTER 
the 'parse arg line' line..

callscript 'Doors:CPS/GetCPS'

It will return to the script you called it from and WILL NOT interrupt
an auto-logoff after up/download with a 'Press ANY KEY...'.  I use a 
delay instead to keep that from happening.

Be sure to install the archive's contents into your Doors: assign.
It should look like this:

Doors:CPS/
     GetCPS.zeus
     CPSData/
          CPSNumbers

     
That's it - it will create it's own files as needed in it's directory
and for the TopCPS chart in the location you choose.


